Match Wine ALSA producer fill/wait order without changing source PCM or clocks.

Wine 10 alsa_timer_loop locks its stream, initializes the QPC deadline,
queries/fills the device, unlocks, and only then performs its first relative
wait. Native slept before its first worker availability query, discarding
that first producer opportunity. Actual forwarded Wine WaveOut evidence has
one RAW clock read before the timer thread's first availability query; the
retained native production Intro has two. Preserve the main-thread initial
fill from Wine alsa_start, move only the worker fill before its wait, and
initialize its QPC deadline under the same stream mutex. Keep clock units,
signed narrowing, correction limits, PCM and source completion unchanged.
Publish failed main startup under the mutex so the newly immediate worker
cannot retry an initial failure before the caller begins cleanup.

